    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-105",
    "content": "8. Emotional Support Phrases — Expanded (Twi)",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-106",
    "content": "\"Metie deɛ woka no, na ɛyɛ nea ɛfata sɛ ɛha wo.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-107",
    "content": "\"Apenimoo mma no bebree te saa nka ɔhaw yi, na woyɛ yie sɛ woreka kyerɛ me.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-108",
    "content": "\"Ɛnyɛ wo nko ara — ma ɔbaa foforɔ a wowɔ w'akyi (wo hokafo, wo busuafoɔ) mmoa wo.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-109",
    "content": "\"Sɛ ɔhaw no kɔ so a, ɛho hia sɛ ɔdɔkota hwɛ wo, na yɛbɛboa wo akɔ hɔ.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-110",
    "content": "\"Ehu anaa ahopopo a wote nka no yɛ deɛ ɛtaa ba wɔ apenimoo mu — ɛnkyerɛ sɛ biribi bɔne reba.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-111",
    "content": "\"Sɛ wopɛ sɛ wokasa kyerɛ obi wɔ w'abusua mu anaa wo yɔnko mu a, ɛbɛboa wo.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-112",
    "content": "9. Closing / Follow-Up Lines (Twi)",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-113",
    "content": "\"Yɛahu deɛ ɛsɛ sɛ woyɛ seesei. Hwɛ so na sɛ biribi sesa a, san bɛkasa kyerɛ me.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-114",
    "content": "\"Kɔ w'ayaresabea nhyiamu a ɛdi hɔ no so, na sɛ biribi foforɔ ba wɔ ntam a, bisa me.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-115",
    "content": "\"Wo akwahosan ho hia yɛn. Yɛbɛtena wo nkyɛn.\"",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-116",
    "content": "10. Notes for Training / QA",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-117",
    "content": "Every Category C and D response must retain the direct instruction to seek in-person care immediately — do not let translation soften the urgency.",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-118",
    "content": "Twi has regional and dialectal variation (Asante Twi vs Akuapem Twi); this draft leans Asante Twi, which is the most widely understood. Confirm which variant your target users speak.",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-119",
    "content": "Medical loanwords (e.g., \"blood pressure,\" \"ultrasound,\" \"HIV\") are often used in English even in Twi speech — keep them in English where a Twi equivalent would confuse users, and pair with a short Twi explanation, as done above.",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "M-CARE_Twi_Knowledge_Base.pdf",
      "language": "tw",
      "type": "clinical-knowledge-base"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "mcare-twi-pdf-120",
